Answer: ```java
public class Main {
static void printSquare(int num1, int num2) {
System.out.println("Square of " + num1 + " is " + (num1 * num1));
System.out.println("Square of " + num2 + " is " + (num2 * num2));
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
printSquare(4, 6);
}
}
```

Sample Input: 4 6 Output: Square of 4 is 16 Square of 6 is 36

Answer: ```java
public class Main {
static void printSquare(int num1, int num2) {
System.out.println(num1 * num1);
System.out.println(num2 * num2);
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
printSquare(4, 6);
}
}
```

There are three local variables: num1 num2 args num1 and num2 are parameters of printSquare(), while args is the parameter of main(). All three are local to their respective methods.
